**a) Flowchart of nested if-else structure**

A nested `if-else` places one `if-else` inside the body of another `if` or `else`.

```
          [Start]
             |
             v
       [Input a, b, c]
             |
             v
        [a >= b?] ----No----> [b >= c?] ----No----> [max = c]
          |Yes                         |Yes
          v                            v
     [a >= c?] ------------------> [max = b]
       |No
       v
   [max = a]
       |
       v
    [Print max]
       |
       v
      [Stop]
```
Logic: if `a >= b`, compare `a` with `c`; otherwise compare `b` with `c`. The largest of the three is selected.

**b) C program to input three integers and display the maximum**

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int a, b, c, max;
    printf("Enter three integers: ");
    scanf("%d %d %d", &a, &b, &c);
    if (a >= b) {
        if (a >= c) max = a;
        else max = c;
    } else {
        if (b >= c) max = b;
        else max = c;
    }
    printf("Maximum number = %d\n", max);
    return 0;
}
```
Example: input `12 7 19` → output `Maximum number = 19`.

